1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:00,940
Hey!

2
00:00:00,970 --> 00:00:02,220
You two are cops, aren't you?

3
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:02,800
You...

4
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:11,750
Let go of me!

5
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:13,350
Your eyebrow is bleeding.

6
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:14,050
Are you alright?

7
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:14,740
I'm fine.

8
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,080
Die, you bastards!

9
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,490
Inspector,

10
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:18,670
stop blaming yourself.

11
00:00:18,890 --> 00:00:21,050
Mungkorn might even be happy
when he wakes up

12
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:23,170
and realizes you...

13
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:25,600
care about him
like you're in love with him.

14
00:00:25,630 --> 00:00:28,340
I'm your love, Inspector Thear?

15
00:00:56,510 --> 00:00:57,200
Perfect.

16
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:22,470
Hey, Thear.

17
00:01:26,710 --> 00:01:28,450
What are you doing at Mungkorn's desk?

18
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:32,580
Well, he left his desk a bit messy,

19
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:34,980
so I'm just helping him tidy up.
That's all.

20
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:42,360
Right, give me a summary
of the Black Bull case tonight.

21
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,310
Can I hand it in tomorrow instead?

22
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:48,890
I happen to have some important business
to take care of today.

23
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:52,340
I have to be at the hospital
to look after Mungkorn.

24
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:55,120
It won't be good if I'm late.

25
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:57,080
Basically,

26
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:00,260
it's not about the business,

27
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,910
but the person.

28
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:07,640
Well, that explains
why you're taking such good care of him.

29
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:12,890
Mungkorn is lucky.
He's got a great boss...

30
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:15,450
and a wonderful husband.

31
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:19,000
Wait a minute, Uncle.

32
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,780
Do you...

33
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:22,760
know about us?

34
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:28,870
If I couldn't figure that out,
how could I be the chief around here?

35
00:02:30,410 --> 00:02:31,150
Okay.

36
00:02:31,890 --> 00:02:33,060
Then get going.

37
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,570
We can talk about the summary
some other time.

38
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,510
Your partner is waiting.

39
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:43,090
He's not just any partner.

40
00:02:44,970 --> 00:02:45,910
He's my husband.

41
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:49,720
I see...

42
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:11,920
Whoa!

43
00:03:12,690 --> 00:03:15,160
See what happens when you don't let me
go undercover as a host?

44
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:16,900
That's how you ended up getting shot.

45
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:18,960
Stop bragging so much.

46
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:20,390
You got yourself hurt, too.

47
00:03:21,850 --> 00:03:23,080
I let my guard down.

48
00:03:23,530 --> 00:03:25,050
Let's just call it a lesson learned.

49
00:03:26,650 --> 00:03:27,830
Anyway, at the very least,

50
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:31,400
we caught a whole bunch
of those Black Bull agents.

51
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,440
But we still haven't gotten their boss.

52
00:03:33,950 --> 00:03:35,690
That Tiannan guy we caught...

53
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,200
is just another underling.

54
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:39,460
I'm not giving up.

55
00:03:40,730 --> 00:03:41,820
No matter what,

56
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:45,050
I have to track them
all the way to the boss.

57
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:46,630
Just take it easy.

58
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,750
Don't push yourself too hard.

59
00:03:54,170 --> 00:03:55,720
Wait until you're fully recovered first.

60
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,210
I'll take care of him.

61
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:00,600
I just hate to let the trail go cold.

62
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:03,680
I feel like
we're getting closer every minute.

63
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:07,480
It's not going to be easy.

64
00:04:08,010 --> 00:04:10,240
These people
have connections everywhere.

65
00:04:12,850 --> 00:04:14,150
They could even have someone in here.

66
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,490
Is it you, Kanin?

67
00:04:17,890 --> 00:04:18,980
Watch what you're saying.

68
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,780
I almost got caught myself,

69
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:22,660
so I had to kiss Nadol
to fool those guys.

70
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:26,420
- You guys kissed?
- You guys kissed?

71
00:04:26,830 --> 00:04:29,720
We did it just to throw them off,

72
00:04:29,990 --> 00:04:32,420
just like how you two tricked Tiannan.

73
00:04:32,450 --> 00:04:33,270
It's pretty much the same.

74
00:04:41,690 --> 00:04:43,000
You'd better watch out for this one

75
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,080
because Kanin was serious about it.

76
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,390
I actually didn't mind.

77
00:04:52,530 --> 00:04:53,590
Well, I certainly did.

78
00:04:55,730 --> 00:04:58,430
Keep bickering,
and you might actually end up together.

79
00:04:58,840 --> 00:04:59,860
I've seen it happen before.

80
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:06,800
I'll go get the door.

81
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:16,370
Saming?

82
00:05:18,330 --> 00:05:19,270
What are you doing here?

83
00:05:22,390 --> 00:05:23,160
Why?

84
00:05:24,050 --> 00:05:25,810
Can't I visit my friend?

85
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:46,060
(Yin as Theartha)

86
00:05:50,990 --> 00:05:53,720
(War as Mungkorn)

87
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:00,210
(Shane as Phuwin)

88
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:03,680
(Boss as Lukplub)

89
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:07,790
(Kit as Kanin)

90
00:06:08,050 --> 00:06:10,000
(Tang as Nadol)

91
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:18,720
(Tae as Saming)

92
00:06:44,990 --> 00:06:46,210
How are you doing, Mungkorn?

93
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:48,100
When I heard that you'd been shot,

94
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,770
I rushed here immediately.

95
00:06:50,130 --> 00:06:51,770
Thank you so much for coming,

96
00:06:51,850 --> 00:06:53,690
but I'm feeling a lot better now.

97
00:06:53,970 --> 00:06:56,090
You shouldn't have troubled yourself
to come all this way.

98
00:06:56,370 --> 00:06:57,410
It's necessary.

99
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:59,150
I was worried sick about you.

100
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:02,850
I wonder how the inspector here
takes care of his men

101
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,800
when he lets one of them
nearly get killed.

102
00:07:06,810 --> 00:07:09,070
Mungkorn, if you were under my wing,

103
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:13,000
I guarantee you wouldn't have
a single scratch on you.

104
00:07:14,290 --> 00:07:15,540
That's not what happened.

105
00:07:16,110 --> 00:07:18,020
I should have been more careful myself.

106
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:22,510
As a cop,
you know these things can happen.

107
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:24,400
It's okay.

108
00:07:25,390 --> 00:07:27,070
Let me take care of you right now, then.

109
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:28,430
Here.

110
00:07:28,890 --> 00:07:31,270
I brought you plenty of stuff
to help you recover.

111
00:07:35,390 --> 00:07:36,400
I don't think that's necessary.

112
00:07:36,780 --> 00:07:38,890
Mungkorn can feed himself.
He doesn't need your help.

113
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:39,920
I know,

114
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:42,070
but I still want to do it for him.

115
00:07:42,790 --> 00:07:44,070
It's not your job.

116
00:07:44,090 --> 00:07:45,270
Then whose job is it?

117
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:46,560
Is it yours?

118
00:07:47,260 --> 00:07:48,210
And why is it yours?

119
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:02,540
It's fine, guys.

120
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,190
I'll eat it myself.

121
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,460
It's really sweet.

122
00:08:27,290 --> 00:08:28,290
Totally organic.

123
00:08:30,890 --> 00:08:33,010
Here, I bought you some coffee.

124
00:08:35,190 --> 00:08:35,990
Thank you.

125
00:08:41,950 --> 00:08:42,800
Captain,

126
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:45,260
how come Inspector Saming from Phayao

127
00:08:45,630 --> 00:08:47,140
knows Mungkorn?

128
00:08:47,570 --> 00:08:50,090
From what I heard,
back when they were students,

129
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:53,650
Thear and Saming were senior volunteers
who served as assistant trainers.

130
00:08:54,020 --> 00:08:55,880
That was exactly
the year Mungkorn joined.

131
00:08:57,660 --> 00:08:59,610
Everyone, right face!

132
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:09,660
He seems genuinely worried
about Mungkorn, though.

133
00:09:10,710 --> 00:09:13,370
Maybe he just wants to mess with Thear.

134
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:13,890
Sh*t.

135
00:09:18,170 --> 00:09:19,430
- You bastard!
- Cut it out!

136
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:21,120
Why are you guys fighting?

137
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,900
Phuwin told me that

138
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:28,410
they've been rivals forever.

139
00:09:33,150 --> 00:09:34,910
But let's not mind them.

140
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:36,930
Let's focus on us instead.

141
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:38,550
What are you talking about?

142
00:09:39,050 --> 00:09:40,950
I'm talking about
the fact that you kissed me.

143
00:09:42,370 --> 00:09:43,230
What about it?

144
00:09:43,250 --> 00:09:45,780
I told you it was just for the mission.

145
00:09:46,530 --> 00:09:47,900
Why are you making a big deal out of it?

146
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:49,320
Whoa...

147
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:51,350
You kissed me,
and now you're ditching me?

148
00:09:51,870 --> 00:09:53,300
Why are you being so dramatic?

149
00:09:53,630 --> 00:09:54,680
I'm not.

150
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,750
But since our lips have met,

151
00:09:56,770 --> 00:09:58,570
I'm considering you off the market.

152
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:01,610
Whatever you say, Captain.

153
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:35,550
(Why didn't you tell me, sweetie?)

154
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:39,430
(Would you have kept it from me
if Saming hadn't told me?)

155
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:41,730
I just didn't want you to worry, Mom.

156
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:44,940
(I'm coming to stay with you
until you're better.)

157
00:10:44,970 --> 00:10:46,480
You don't need to, Mom.

158
00:10:46,610 --> 00:10:48,680
It's a long way.
It'll be too much trouble for you.

159
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:51,620
Don't worry, Mom.

160
00:10:51,830 --> 00:10:53,730
I'll look after Mungkorn for you.

161
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,530
(Thank you, Saming.)

162
00:10:55,710 --> 00:10:57,080
(I'm counting on you.)

163
00:10:57,230 --> 00:10:59,960
(Can I talk to Inspector Thear
for a second?)

164
00:11:02,490 --> 00:11:03,290
Thear.

165
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:04,750
What?

166
00:11:06,310 --> 00:11:08,090
Mungkorn's mom wants to talk to you.

167
00:11:11,670 --> 00:11:13,810
You should leave
so Mungkorn can get some rest.

168
00:11:24,390 --> 00:11:25,370
Hello, Mom.

169
00:11:26,130 --> 00:11:27,000
(Inspector...)

170
00:11:27,490 --> 00:11:29,510
(Why didn't you tell me...)

171
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:31,500
(about Mungkorn being shot?)

172
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:32,860
Oh...

173
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:37,130
Mungkorn asked me not to.

174
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:38,540
He was worried you'd be upset.

175
00:11:38,570 --> 00:11:40,300
(That's still not right.)

176
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:42,040
(He's my only son.)

177
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:44,840
(I allowed my son to marry you,)

178
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:47,290
(so you must take good care of him.)

179
00:11:47,490 --> 00:11:50,130
(Mungkorn is my heart.)

180
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:52,610
(You have to look after him)

181
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:55,080
(as if you were
looking after your own heart.)

182
00:11:55,110 --> 00:11:56,410
- Had to get it removed.
- (Do you understand?)

183
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:58,250
Of course, Mom.

184
00:11:58,950 --> 00:12:00,100
From now on,

185
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:02,780
I will protect Mungkorn with my life.

186
00:12:29,150 --> 00:12:30,700
This is so frustrating.

187
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,210
So annoying.

188
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:33,760
If you keep sighing like that,

189
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,860
you're going to die young,

190
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:38,080
since you're not
exactly young anymore.

191
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:40,900
Fine, just let me die.

192
00:12:46,820 --> 00:12:47,480
Hey.

193
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:49,920
What's wrong, Inspector?

194
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:54,480
What did you just call me?

195
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:56,470
Inspector...

196
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:58,880
What did you say?

197
00:12:59,270 --> 00:13:00,150
Inspector.

198
00:13:01,050 --> 00:13:02,970
If you don't call me what you used to,

199
00:13:04,290 --> 00:13:06,890
I'll let out the biggest sigh
the whole world can hear.

200
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:13,520
Thear!

201
00:13:14,370 --> 00:13:15,440
Happy now?

202
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:18,780
I guess so.

203
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,910
So, why all the sighing?

204
00:13:25,650 --> 00:13:28,740
Did my mom say something to upset you?

205
00:13:29,290 --> 00:13:30,080
No.

206
00:13:30,590 --> 00:13:31,880
She didn't say anything bad.

207
00:13:32,790 --> 00:13:34,440
She just told me
to take good care of you.

208
00:13:34,870 --> 00:13:36,260
Since I've married her son,

209
00:13:36,390 --> 00:13:38,740
I have to look after
both his life and his heart.

210
00:13:42,180 --> 00:13:44,220
My mom is just overprotective.

211
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:46,460
Don't overthink it.

212
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,430
But that's not the point.

213
00:13:55,660 --> 00:13:57,050
Then what is it?

214
00:13:59,770 --> 00:14:00,900
It's you.

215
00:14:01,570 --> 00:14:03,000
Ever since Saming showed up,

216
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:04,360
I've been cast aside like a stray dog.

217
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:06,210
Why were you so happy to see him?

218
00:14:06,870 --> 00:14:07,700
Well...

219
00:14:08,210 --> 00:14:10,230
I haven't seen him in such a long time.

220
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:11,750
Should I have been scowling?

221
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:13,170
I had to smile.

222
00:14:13,810 --> 00:14:14,640
Whatever you say,

223
00:14:14,670 --> 00:14:17,620
but was it really necessary
to let him feed you fruit like that?

224
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,610
If he's feeding me, I have to...

225
00:14:19,970 --> 00:14:20,990
I have to eat it.

226
00:14:23,210 --> 00:14:24,650
You want me to swat it away?

227
00:14:25,830 --> 00:14:27,200
Whoa.

228
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,660
Always taking his side, huh?

229
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:30,050
You never agree to anything I say.

230
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:36,970
Look.

231
00:14:38,230 --> 00:14:41,140
Are you being jealous or just mad?

232
00:14:43,230 --> 00:14:44,190
That's right.

233
00:14:44,410 --> 00:14:45,090
I'm jealous.

234
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:46,350
Very jealous.

235
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:48,980
My husband...

236
00:14:49,090 --> 00:14:50,430
I can take care of him myself.

237
00:14:52,890 --> 00:14:53,590
Hey.

238
00:14:54,570 --> 00:14:55,710
- Ow...
- Whoa, whoa.

239
00:14:56,050 --> 00:14:57,050
Sorry. Did I hit it?

240
00:14:57,130 --> 00:14:58,050
I'm okay.

241
00:15:01,250 --> 00:15:02,660
I just wanted to say...

242
00:15:02,950 --> 00:15:04,480
it doesn't matter what others think.

243
00:15:04,510 --> 00:15:05,640
I don't care.

244
00:15:06,310 --> 00:15:07,910
I'm married,

245
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:10,550
and the only one I care about
is you, Thear.

246
00:15:17,470 --> 00:15:19,220
You're staying here tonight.

247
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:22,680
You're distracted right now.
I can't let you go home alone.

248
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:25,410
You'll probably end up
back in the hospital somehow.

249
00:15:25,930 --> 00:15:27,230
Your mom will be worried.

250
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:33,050
I have one small problem.

251
00:15:33,110 --> 00:15:35,460
It's cold sleeping on the couch.

252
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:40,050
Then sleep on the bed.
I'll sleep on the couch.

253
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:41,610
Just kidding.

254
00:15:42,730 --> 00:15:43,570
It's fine.

255
00:15:43,590 --> 00:15:46,610
Just being able to look at your face
is enough to keep me warm.

256
00:15:48,110 --> 00:15:49,280
Couch it is.

257
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:57,990
Are you sure?

258
00:15:58,540 --> 00:15:59,390
Would you be alright?

259
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:00,220
It's fine.

260
00:16:00,650 --> 00:16:02,100
Slowly.

261
00:16:42,570 --> 00:16:43,550
What are you doing?

262
00:16:44,050 --> 00:16:45,070
A sponge bath?

263
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:46,510
Yes.

264
00:16:46,930 --> 00:16:48,470
Please let me do it, then.

265
00:16:49,350 --> 00:16:50,700
What are you talking about?

266
00:16:51,210 --> 00:16:53,680
Let the nurse do it. It's her job.

267
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:56,290
But as your husband, it's my job

268
00:16:56,610 --> 00:16:58,350
to take care of you
when you're not well.

269
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:00,710
Isn't that right?

270
00:17:00,850 --> 00:17:01,940
Yes, that's right.

271
00:17:02,070 --> 00:17:02,970
Exactly.

272
00:17:03,870 --> 00:17:05,530
In that case, please go ahead.

273
00:17:06,490 --> 00:17:07,760
I'll just leave things as they were.

274
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:08,460
Okay.

275
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:10,220
Please, go ahead.

276
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:12,350
- Thank you so much.
- You're welcome.

277
00:17:13,430 --> 00:17:14,550
I feel like a third wheel.

278
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:16,730
I've got you a flower

279
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:18,010
to brighten things up.

280
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:20,230
Thank you.

281
00:17:23,310 --> 00:17:24,950
Oh, are you shy around me?

282
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:29,410
I've already seen all of you.

283
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:31,930
I know.

284
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:34,480
Anyway, I'm still not used to it.

285
00:17:36,390 --> 00:17:37,620
You'd better get used to it

286
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:39,830
because from now on,

287
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:42,270
I'm going to give you a sponge bath
every single day

288
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:43,890
until you're fully recovered.

289
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:25,460
I'm going to lift it slowly.

290
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:28,070
How's this?

291
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:36,770
It hurts?

292
00:19:37,630 --> 00:19:38,850
Is it okay if I keep going?

293
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:40,470
- Keep going, Inspector.
- Okay.

294
00:19:40,690 --> 00:19:41,320
Here we go!

295
00:19:44,130 --> 00:19:45,940
Hang in there. Look at me. Stay strong.

296
00:19:46,430 --> 00:19:47,500
Okay, all the way!

297
00:19:50,370 --> 00:19:51,740
Take deep breaths, Mungkorn.

298
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:55,390
Can you handle it?

299
00:19:55,950 --> 00:19:56,680
Yeah.

300
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:57,640
How does it feel?

301
00:19:58,170 --> 00:19:59,580
- Relaxing?
- We should change positions.

302
00:19:59,850 --> 00:20:00,940
- Let's try another one.
- Oh...

303
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:05,590
This is a hospital. What are you doing?

304
00:20:07,150 --> 00:20:08,020
Just some stretching.

305
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:09,280
Right...

306
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,270
- Oh, okay.
- No worries. Thank you very much.

307
00:20:12,290 --> 00:20:13,320
You can just leave it there.

308
00:20:13,710 --> 00:20:14,790
Here's your evening medication.

309
00:20:14,850 --> 00:20:15,960
Yes, thank you.

310
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:16,800
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

311
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:19,800
Shall we keep going?

312
00:20:19,830 --> 00:20:20,500
Yes.

313
00:20:21,350 --> 00:20:22,390
Bend your knee for this one.

314
00:20:22,570 --> 00:20:23,650
Bend your knee.

315
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:26,440
Listen.

316
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:27,900
It hurts, doesn't it?

317
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,210
It does.

318
00:20:39,590 --> 00:20:40,430
Oh, hey.

319
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:41,520
How are you feeling?

320
00:20:41,950 --> 00:20:43,090
Ready to get back to work?

321
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:43,770
Yes, sir.

322
00:20:43,990 --> 00:20:46,060
I am Sergeant Mungkorn Phianwanich,

323
00:20:46,170 --> 00:20:48,230
ready to serve the people!

324
00:20:49,530 --> 00:20:50,870
Whoa, what's all this?

325
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:53,360
Is the wound opening up?

326
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:54,910
Let me see.

327
00:20:57,650 --> 00:20:58,800
It doesn't hurt too much, does it?

328
00:20:58,870 --> 00:20:59,710
No, it's fine.

329
00:21:00,690 --> 00:21:02,050
Let's not play around just yet.

330
00:21:02,330 --> 00:21:03,440
Your wound has only just healed.

331
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:04,370
Understood.

332
00:21:08,650 --> 00:21:09,770
Thank you, Thear,

333
00:21:10,290 --> 00:21:11,970
for looking after me
for the last three weeks.

334
00:21:15,430 --> 00:21:16,330
Well, I told you

335
00:21:16,990 --> 00:21:19,320
that I'm the perfect husband.

336
00:21:41,110 --> 00:21:42,820
All healed up, right?

337
00:21:43,330 --> 00:21:46,450
You can continue your recovery at home

338
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:49,220
as we're out of ant killer
at the hospital.

339
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:51,960
Apparently, the ants couldn't handle
all this sweetness.

340
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:54,650
Thank you so much, Miss Pretty Nurse.

341
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:55,350
You're welcome.

342
00:21:55,540 --> 00:21:57,110
Come on. Let's go.

343
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:01,490
Let's go.

344
00:22:01,950 --> 00:22:02,980
- Goodbye.
- Thank you.

345
00:22:03,010 --> 00:22:03,910
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

346
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:12,570
Must be nice
to be so good-looking and loved.

347
00:22:14,100 --> 00:22:15,140
My goodness.

348
00:22:24,540 --> 00:22:26,650
Wait, aren't we going back to our place?

349
00:22:26,970 --> 00:22:28,390
My, my.

350
00:22:28,900 --> 00:22:31,210
Are you already comfortable
calling my house "our place"?

351
00:22:32,030 --> 00:22:32,830
I'm so happy.

352
00:22:33,670 --> 00:22:35,720
I brought you here to keep my promise.

353
00:22:36,060 --> 00:22:37,320
I said if you made it through,

354
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:39,500
we'd come have shaved ice
at your favorite place.

355
00:22:41,380 --> 00:22:43,480
Actually, the place is closed today,

356
00:22:44,290 --> 00:22:45,980
but I booked the whole place out

357
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:47,350
just for you.

358
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:48,860
Are you for real?

359
00:22:49,670 --> 00:22:51,270
You went to all that trouble?

360
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:52,800
For you...

361
00:22:53,190 --> 00:22:54,690
I'd do even more.

362
00:22:58,370 --> 00:22:59,720
Come on, let's eat.

363
00:23:09,790 --> 00:23:10,990
- Hello!
- Hello.

364
00:23:11,020 --> 00:23:12,270
What would you like today?

365
00:23:12,820 --> 00:23:14,510
I'll have the grass jelly,
sugar palm seeds,

366
00:23:14,540 --> 00:23:17,570
and a mix of red and green syrups
with lots of condensed milk, please.

367
00:23:17,650 --> 00:23:18,300
Coming right up.

368
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,250
Whoa,

369
00:23:19,330 --> 00:23:21,160
adding all these extras
and lots of condensed milk?

370
00:23:21,740 --> 00:23:23,560
Are you really
that deprived of sweetness?

371
00:23:24,010 --> 00:23:25,730
I thought I'd given you
enough of that already.

372
00:23:26,250 --> 00:23:27,860
Guess it's still not enough.

373
00:23:28,230 --> 00:23:30,520
I'll have to be
your personal sugar factory, then.

374
00:23:31,350 --> 00:23:32,610
This is plenty.

375
00:23:32,930 --> 00:23:33,970
I don't want to end up with diabetes.

376
00:23:35,470 --> 00:23:36,570
We'll take two, please.

377
00:23:36,930 --> 00:23:39,080
Would you like anything else?

378
00:23:39,590 --> 00:23:41,010
No, I'm good.

379
00:23:41,820 --> 00:23:44,020
What about this one?
Don't you want him?

380
00:23:46,110 --> 00:23:46,940
This one...

381
00:23:47,990 --> 00:23:49,830
He'd take it home with him.

382
00:23:50,970 --> 00:23:52,430
Did you tell her to say that?

383
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:53,540
What do you mean?

384
00:23:53,990 --> 00:23:55,740
She can see for herself
that we're a couple.

385
00:23:56,290 --> 00:23:57,300
She's just teasing us.

386
00:23:57,780 --> 00:23:58,790
Isn't that right?

387
00:23:59,080 --> 00:23:59,930
That's right.

388
00:24:00,220 --> 00:24:01,420
No need to be shy.

389
00:24:07,870 --> 00:24:08,580
Ow!

390
00:24:09,330 --> 00:24:09,930
What's wrong?

391
00:24:11,730 --> 00:24:12,860
Brain freeze.

392
00:24:14,150 --> 00:24:16,530
You ate it too fast.
That's why you got a brain freeze.

393
00:24:17,770 --> 00:24:19,570
Is it really that good?

394
00:24:20,060 --> 00:24:21,230
Did you have to eat it that quickly?

395
00:24:22,210 --> 00:24:23,210
It is good.

396
00:24:23,670 --> 00:24:25,260
It makes me feel so much better.

397
00:24:25,630 --> 00:24:26,750
When I was in the hospital,

398
00:24:27,290 --> 00:24:28,640
I had to eat the same food every day.

399
00:24:32,780 --> 00:24:34,290
If there's anything you want to eat

400
00:24:34,470 --> 00:24:35,530
or anywhere you'd like to go,

401
00:24:35,820 --> 00:24:36,860
just let me know.

402
00:24:37,410 --> 00:24:39,520
I took the day off today
specifically to take care of you.

403
00:24:40,490 --> 00:24:41,620
Come on, Thear.

404
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:43,910
I can take care of myself now.

405
00:24:44,310 --> 00:24:46,390
I know you can,

406
00:24:46,670 --> 00:24:47,900
but I want to do it for you.

407
00:24:48,900 --> 00:24:50,550
Come on, just let me.

408
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:53,840
Fine.

409
00:24:56,780 --> 00:24:59,030
So, is there anywhere you want to go?

410
00:25:00,130 --> 00:25:00,880
Yeah.

411
00:25:01,450 --> 00:25:02,950
I want to go to a temple
and pay my respects.

412
00:25:03,310 --> 00:25:05,450
I've been having
some seriously bad luck lately.

413
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:07,340
Alright.

414
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:09,170
Let's go make merit together,

415
00:25:09,890 --> 00:25:10,990
and from now on,

416
00:25:11,190 --> 00:25:13,030
we'll both be lucky.

417
00:25:27,610 --> 00:25:28,590
Are you doing okay?

418
00:25:28,860 --> 00:25:30,150
It's still quite a long way.

419
00:25:30,940 --> 00:25:32,730
You should've taken the cable car
like I told you to.

420
00:25:34,190 --> 00:25:35,750
No need. I'm fine.

421
00:25:35,870 --> 00:25:36,750
After all,

422
00:25:37,190 --> 00:25:39,430
I need to get some exercise.

423
00:25:39,940 --> 00:25:40,810
Are you sure you're fine?

424
00:25:41,050 --> 00:25:41,670
Yeah.

425
00:25:41,690 --> 00:25:43,510
- Let me carry you up.
- No way, stop it.

426
00:25:43,730 --> 00:25:44,660
I'll walk by myself.

427
00:25:48,910 --> 00:25:50,110
Whoa, whoa!

428
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:55,650
See?

429
00:25:56,170 --> 00:25:57,270
I told you so.

430
00:25:57,550 --> 00:25:58,420
You're not going to make it.

431
00:25:58,460 --> 00:25:59,660
Let me help you up.

432
00:26:01,290 --> 00:26:02,090
Fine, then.

433
00:26:06,740 --> 00:26:07,440
So stubborn.

434
00:26:10,830 --> 00:26:12,820
If I fell from here, I'd break my neck.

435
00:26:17,210 --> 00:26:19,850
My name is Theartha Phiromsamorn.

436
00:26:20,220 --> 00:26:22,670
My name is Mungkorn Phianwanich...

437
00:26:23,250 --> 00:26:25,010
- From this day forward,
- From this day forward...

438
00:26:29,750 --> 00:26:33,120
may there be
no more hardship or harm in our lives.

439
00:26:33,850 --> 00:26:35,430
May we never get hurt again.

440
00:26:36,030 --> 00:26:40,470
And may we live happily
for many years to come.

441
00:27:09,120 --> 00:27:10,100
What's wrong?

442
00:27:10,510 --> 00:27:11,800
I stepped on a lit incense stick.

443
00:27:13,350 --> 00:27:14,380
Let's go sit down first.

444
00:27:19,260 --> 00:27:21,130
- Hang in there. Take a seat.
- Ow, it stings!

445
00:27:22,510 --> 00:27:23,450
It burns!

446
00:27:24,010 --> 00:27:25,010
Let me have a look.

447
00:27:27,170 --> 00:27:28,180
It's really red.

448
00:27:32,260 --> 00:27:33,230
Let's cool it down first...

449
00:27:35,550 --> 00:27:37,310
so it won't blister too badly.

450
00:27:38,340 --> 00:27:39,250
Thank you.

451
00:27:43,900 --> 00:27:44,590
How are you feeling?

452
00:27:44,930 --> 00:27:46,610
Will you be able to walk down?

453
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:47,920
I'm fine. Look, it's gone.

454
00:27:48,140 --> 00:27:49,410
Whoa, seriously?

455
00:27:52,240 --> 00:27:53,520
I stepped right on it.

456
00:27:57,380 --> 00:28:01,030
Seeing you kids so in love
really warms my heart.

457
00:28:03,230 --> 00:28:04,170
By the way,

458
00:28:04,830 --> 00:28:06,420
I've got a story to tell you.

459
00:28:06,830 --> 00:28:09,440
There's a legend about this place.

460
00:28:10,070 --> 00:28:11,600
What kind of legend, sir?

461
00:28:12,040 --> 00:28:14,140
The legend says...

462
00:28:14,820 --> 00:28:16,850
if a couple isn't meant to be

463
00:28:16,870 --> 00:28:19,800
and they come up here to worship
at Doi Suthep,

464
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:23,150
they'll end up breaking up
once they go back down.

465
00:28:24,260 --> 00:28:26,350
Why do people believe that?

466
00:28:27,430 --> 00:28:29,680
It's been a legend since the old days.

467
00:28:29,710 --> 00:28:32,480
Back then, the path up here
was just a dirt trail,

468
00:28:32,760 --> 00:28:36,720
and between the heat,
the rain, and the wind,

469
00:28:37,020 --> 00:28:38,520
they'd end up arguing on the way down

470
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:39,500
and breaking up.

471
00:28:42,280 --> 00:28:42,880
Sir,

472
00:28:43,140 --> 00:28:45,430
the two of us won't be breaking up.

473
00:28:45,610 --> 00:28:46,660
We're already married.

474
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:47,320
What?

475
00:28:47,540 --> 00:28:50,080
Oh, then I must apologize.

476
00:28:50,120 --> 00:28:52,840
You're married? Well, congratulations.

477
00:28:53,020 --> 00:28:57,040
I wish you both a long life together
until you're old and gray.

478
00:28:57,790 --> 00:28:59,310
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

479
00:28:59,330 --> 00:29:00,190
My pleasure.

480
00:29:00,260 --> 00:29:01,950
I'll get back to work now.

481
00:29:02,730 --> 00:29:03,610
- Sure thing.
- Take care.

482
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:15,530
Don't pay any mind to those legends.

483
00:29:16,510 --> 00:29:17,830
Whether people break up or not

484
00:29:17,980 --> 00:29:18,830
depends on the people,

485
00:29:19,040 --> 00:29:20,260
not the place.

486
00:29:22,860 --> 00:29:23,820
Besides,

487
00:29:24,410 --> 00:29:26,080
aren't we soulmates?

488
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:30,180
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

489
00:29:30,770 --> 00:29:33,460
We still have a lot to prove
in the long run.

490
00:29:37,430 --> 00:29:38,320
So you're all better?

491
00:29:38,350 --> 00:29:39,120
Yeah, I'm fine.

492
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:41,160
I don't get to carry you down
on my back, then.

493
00:29:42,580 --> 00:29:43,700
All those hundreds of steps?

494
00:29:44,480 --> 00:29:45,280
I can handle it.

495
00:30:06,460 --> 00:30:08,060
Whose house are you taking me to?

496
00:30:09,680 --> 00:30:11,520
You mentioned wanting to buy a house
for your mom,

497
00:30:11,550 --> 00:30:12,500
so I brought you here.

498
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:15,420
I could never afford this.

499
00:30:15,940 --> 00:30:17,320
I could only dream of it.

500
00:30:17,680 --> 00:30:18,740
Just take a look first.

501
00:30:19,140 --> 00:30:21,480
If you still want it
after these six months are up,

502
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:23,630
I'll buy it for you.

503
00:30:34,640 --> 00:30:36,790
Come on, let this sugar daddy
show you around.

504
00:30:39,660 --> 00:30:44,220
♪Hold my hand
and I'll lead the way, my moonlight♪

505
00:30:44,240 --> 00:30:48,820
♪I'll tell my grandma and the buffalo
you're mine tonight♪

506
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:52,830
♪And my heart will belong to you
for the rest of my life♪

507
00:30:56,530 --> 00:30:57,700
Pretty comfy, right?

508
00:30:59,670 --> 00:31:00,860
Whoa, this is really comfy.

509
00:31:01,090 --> 00:31:02,440
Thear, what are you doing?

510
00:31:02,950 --> 00:31:04,200
Someone might see us.

511
00:31:06,140 --> 00:31:07,240
Now that you've seen the show house

512
00:31:07,260 --> 00:31:10,700
and the surroundings
at Supalai Tuscany Valley, Chiang Mai,

513
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:11,950
what do you think?

514
00:31:11,980 --> 00:31:15,360
Do you feel the design and living space
meet your family's needs?

515
00:31:15,380 --> 00:31:17,120
It absolutely fits
what we're looking for.

516
00:31:17,460 --> 00:31:18,840
I'll bring my mom to see it sometime.

517
00:31:21,250 --> 00:31:23,530
I bet my mom would love this room.

518
00:31:23,660 --> 00:31:24,620
The living room.

519
00:31:28,010 --> 00:31:29,710
Should we bring her here to see it?

520
00:31:30,330 --> 00:31:31,580
Whoa, right now?

521
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:41,900
I'm trying to see if we could do this.

522
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:44,560
The couch is quite spacious, though.

523
00:31:52,410 --> 00:31:54,210
Alright, Khaomao. How do I cut this?

524
00:31:55,750 --> 00:31:57,490
To cut vegetables,
you start from the tips.

525
00:31:57,510 --> 00:31:58,950
Use only the tender parts!

526
00:31:59,230 --> 00:32:01,130
- Cut them into bite-sized pieces.
- Is this about right?

527
00:32:01,240 --> 00:32:03,320
That's too small. Make it bigger.

528
00:32:03,330 --> 00:32:03,940
Okay.

529
00:32:03,940 --> 00:32:05,430
- Don't be so harsh.
- Oh.

530
00:32:05,460 --> 00:32:05,940
How's this?

531
00:32:05,940 --> 00:32:07,420
- Yeah, that's good.
- Okay.

532
00:32:08,950 --> 00:32:09,500
Like this?

533
00:32:09,520 --> 00:32:11,090
- Yes, exactly.
- Okay.

534
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:12,010
That part's not tender.

535
00:32:12,170 --> 00:32:14,180
- Yeah, only the tips.
- Wait, we're not using this at all?

536
00:32:14,340 --> 00:32:15,180
Only the tips.

537
00:32:15,720 --> 00:32:16,770
You keep forgetting your place.

538
00:32:16,930 --> 00:32:18,380
You're gonna get fired.

539
00:32:18,410 --> 00:32:19,960
- He's Lady's son!
- Oh, right.

540
00:32:32,470 --> 00:32:34,510
Okay, the veggies are in. What's next?

541
00:32:34,540 --> 00:32:36,080
I'll let Khaopuk cut the shallots...

542
00:32:36,290 --> 00:32:37,810
Khaopuk, let me do it myself.

543
00:32:37,850 --> 00:32:38,680
- Sorry?
- Give it to me.

544
00:32:38,700 --> 00:32:39,260
Oh...

545
00:32:39,860 --> 00:32:40,760
Be my guest.

546
00:32:42,480 --> 00:32:43,080
Do I cut it?

547
00:32:43,100 --> 00:32:44,400
- Yes.
- Do we need much more?

548
00:32:44,420 --> 00:32:46,500
Obviously, we're making a huge portion.

549
00:32:47,140 --> 00:32:48,920
Right, and make them smaller.

550
00:32:49,670 --> 00:32:51,030
Cut them evenly,

551
00:32:51,060 --> 00:32:52,880
or they won't cook at the same time.

552
00:32:57,480 --> 00:32:58,540
Watch your tone.

553
00:32:58,570 --> 00:32:59,520
What are you doing, Thear?

554
00:32:59,550 --> 00:33:00,100
Whoa!

555
00:33:00,120 --> 00:33:01,280
Hey, hey!

556
00:33:01,840 --> 00:33:03,690
I told you not to come down yet.

557
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:05,190
Now the surprise is ruined.

558
00:33:05,820 --> 00:33:06,990
Why are you in the kitchen?

559
00:33:07,320 --> 00:33:09,310
Aren't you afraid of your luck tanking
like last time?

560
00:33:09,870 --> 00:33:10,770
I am,

561
00:33:11,020 --> 00:33:11,850
but...

562
00:33:12,220 --> 00:33:13,840
I'd rather cook something for you.

563
00:33:16,410 --> 00:33:17,610
So what are you making?

564
00:33:19,020 --> 00:33:20,490
Tamarind, vegetables...

565
00:33:21,020 --> 00:33:22,330
Are you making jor pak kad?

566
00:33:23,300 --> 00:33:25,700
Wow, that's my favorite
whenever I'm sick.

567
00:33:26,110 --> 00:33:27,700
So you know
how to cook Northern food now?

568
00:33:27,770 --> 00:33:29,190
To be honest, I don't,

569
00:33:29,260 --> 00:33:31,880
but I had Khaomao and Khaopuk teach me.

570
00:33:32,540 --> 00:33:34,580
I did all the seasoning, though.

571
00:33:35,100 --> 00:33:36,920
Not sure if it'll be to your taste.

572
00:33:37,500 --> 00:33:38,910
Then let me do the honors and taste it.

573
00:33:45,100 --> 00:33:46,880
So, does it look appetizing?

574
00:33:46,900 --> 00:33:47,700
It does.

575
00:33:49,020 --> 00:33:50,640
- Careful, it's hot.
- Got it.

576
00:33:52,420 --> 00:33:53,420
They were gone for a whole month,

577
00:33:53,440 --> 00:33:55,300
and now they're even more in love.

578
00:33:55,950 --> 00:33:58,310
I thought Lady was about to
get a new son-in-law.

579
00:33:58,330 --> 00:34:00,650
- Goodness!
- Careful, it's hot.

580
00:34:01,800 --> 00:34:03,480
No need for the palm sugar anymore.

581
00:34:03,500 --> 00:34:04,650
- So sweet.
- Watch out!

582
00:34:04,670 --> 00:34:06,260
They're so in love.

583
00:34:10,280 --> 00:34:11,350
Looking good.

584
00:34:35,710 --> 00:34:36,370
Poof!

585
00:34:37,560 --> 00:34:38,250
Did that help?

586
00:34:38,640 --> 00:34:39,880
- It feels better now.
- Hey!

587
00:34:41,610 --> 00:34:42,490
I don't think that was enough.

588
00:34:43,300 --> 00:34:45,030
I have a special remedy.
Want to try it?

589
00:34:45,350 --> 00:34:46,710
A special remedy? Where is it?

590
00:34:53,510 --> 00:34:54,280
Feeling better?

591
00:34:54,740 --> 00:34:56,630
Oh, that look tells me
that wasn't enough.

592
00:34:57,390 --> 00:34:58,800
I think you need some more.

593
00:35:04,890 --> 00:35:06,810
It's actually working.

594
00:35:07,360 --> 00:35:08,500
Might need a little more.

595
00:35:13,070 --> 00:35:14,670
My hand is what's hurting,
not my cheek!

596
00:35:16,650 --> 00:35:18,310
But did it work?

597
00:35:22,640 --> 00:35:23,930
Come to think of it,

598
00:35:24,490 --> 00:35:25,990
ever since we got married,

599
00:35:27,190 --> 00:35:28,770
my luck has gone downhill.

600
00:35:30,840 --> 00:35:32,560
First I got drugged,

601
00:35:32,950 --> 00:35:34,160
then I fell down the stairs,

602
00:35:34,450 --> 00:35:35,350
got shot,

603
00:35:35,380 --> 00:35:37,220
and now I got scalded.

604
00:35:38,880 --> 00:35:40,990
Looks like your bad luck
finally wore off.

605
00:35:41,490 --> 00:35:42,870
I'm the one stuck with it now.

606
00:35:45,550 --> 00:35:46,350
It's all red.

607
00:35:46,900 --> 00:35:48,470
I'm sure that's not it.

608
00:35:48,740 --> 00:35:51,200
It's probably just a coincidence.

609
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:00,920
Oh, my God!

610
00:36:01,070 --> 00:36:01,730
Mungkorn!

611
00:36:04,190 --> 00:36:05,400
Whoa, whoa!

612
00:36:08,480 --> 00:36:09,230
What's wrong?

613
00:36:09,700 --> 00:36:10,850
I stepped on a lit incense stick.

614
00:36:18,700 --> 00:36:19,440
You bastards!

615
00:36:22,500 --> 00:36:23,120
Hey...

616
00:36:25,750 --> 00:36:26,480
Mungkorn!

617
00:36:39,120 --> 00:36:42,160
(Mother Tongnuan's Shrine)

618
00:36:42,990 --> 00:36:43,840
Excuse me.

619
00:36:46,670 --> 00:36:47,770
Good afternoon, Mother.

620
00:36:51,040 --> 00:36:52,030
See?

621
00:36:52,660 --> 00:36:55,890
I knew you'd eventually come back to me.

622
00:36:56,240 --> 00:36:58,090
You knew this was going to happen,
didn't you?

623
00:37:00,020 --> 00:37:01,400
I'm just an oracle.

624
00:37:02,340 --> 00:37:04,370
How could I possibly read your mind?

625
00:37:05,450 --> 00:37:07,310
Ask whatever it is you want to know.

626
00:37:10,200 --> 00:37:11,730
Since we got married,

627
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:13,440
my luck has actually been improving,

628
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:17,400
but why is it Mungkorn
who's having all the bad luck instead?

629
00:37:18,880 --> 00:37:21,740
Why else do you think
it's called soul-binding?

630
00:37:22,460 --> 00:37:25,830
Once you've made your vows,

631
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:30,640
your lives will counterbalance
each other like a pair of scales.

632
00:37:32,490 --> 00:37:33,660
When one rises,

633
00:37:35,940 --> 00:37:37,350
the other shall fall.

634
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:44,840
Why didn't you tell me this
from the beginning?

635
00:37:45,360 --> 00:37:48,820
I told you already.
You are meant to live as one.

636
00:37:49,150 --> 00:37:52,030
Yet you have heeded none of my words.

637
00:37:52,150 --> 00:37:54,580
The heaven and earth
do not acknowledge your love.

638
00:37:54,960 --> 00:37:56,380
Don't you dare blame me.

639
00:38:34,300 --> 00:38:36,390
Good morning, Thear.

640
00:38:52,820 --> 00:38:54,650
Did you see the gardener next door?

641
00:38:54,680 --> 00:38:55,490
Why? What is it?

642
00:38:55,680 --> 00:38:57,600
I really have to hand it
to the boss.

643
00:38:57,630 --> 00:38:58,210
Yeah?

644
00:38:58,230 --> 00:38:58,960
Short, but...

645
00:38:58,980 --> 00:39:00,860
Oh! Good morning, Mr. Mungkorn.

646
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:02,030
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

647
00:39:02,060 --> 00:39:03,230
Where is Inspector Thear?

648
00:39:03,460 --> 00:39:04,970
He left in the early morning.

649
00:39:05,740 --> 00:39:07,730
To pick up someone important
at the airport.

650
00:39:08,570 --> 00:39:09,140
Someone important...

651
00:39:09,190 --> 00:39:10,170
Someone important?

652
00:39:25,900 --> 00:39:27,190
You're here early...

653
00:39:30,650 --> 00:39:31,330
Inspector...

654
00:39:34,240 --> 00:39:34,840
Belle,

655
00:39:35,610 --> 00:39:36,810
this is Sergeant Mungkorn,

656
00:39:37,070 --> 00:39:38,020
my subordinate.

657
00:39:38,420 --> 00:39:40,120
He was transferred from Mae Sai Station.

658
00:39:40,290 --> 00:39:42,390
He'll be transferred back soon.

659
00:39:42,490 --> 00:39:43,240
I see.

660
00:39:43,650 --> 00:39:44,570
Hello.

661
00:39:45,130 --> 00:39:46,060
Hello.

662
00:39:47,030 --> 00:39:47,800
Wow, Belle.

663
00:39:48,250 --> 00:39:50,520
It's been a while.
You've gotten so much prettier.

664
00:39:50,770 --> 00:39:52,520
Uncle, stop it.

665
00:39:52,580 --> 00:39:54,470
I've always been just as pretty.

666
00:39:55,620 --> 00:39:57,230
I really missed this place.

667
00:39:57,930 --> 00:40:01,860
Did you miss the place
or the person who's here?

668
00:40:03,860 --> 00:40:04,840
Exactly.

669
00:40:05,030 --> 00:40:08,670
So, are you two
going to get back together?

670
00:40:08,890 --> 00:40:10,240
Everyone is rooting for you.

671
00:40:10,310 --> 00:40:10,980
- Come on!
- Are you?

672
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:12,820
What are you talking about, Uncle?

673
00:40:13,330 --> 00:40:15,470
You shouldn't be asking me that.

674
00:40:15,670 --> 00:40:17,310
A lot of people here
are shipping you two.

675
00:40:17,880 --> 00:40:19,620
Since he broke up with you,

676
00:40:19,650 --> 00:40:22,150
I haven't seen a single person
who could handle him.

677
00:40:22,470 --> 00:40:24,320
- Only you can keep him in line.
- Right.

678
00:40:25,160 --> 00:40:27,570
Well, it's not my place
to make the decision.

679
00:40:28,550 --> 00:40:31,090
Then let me ask the gentleman.

680
00:40:31,450 --> 00:40:32,550
The groom...

681
00:40:32,570 --> 00:40:34,140
I mean, Inspector.

682
00:40:34,580 --> 00:40:35,880
So, what's going on here?

683
00:40:36,780 --> 00:40:39,030
We'll just have to wait and see.

684
00:40:39,170 --> 00:40:40,390
Hey!

685
00:40:46,220 --> 00:40:47,330
I knew it.

686
00:40:47,360 --> 00:40:48,870
The person you're wearing that ring for

687
00:40:48,890 --> 00:40:50,920
had to be someone familiar.

688
00:40:51,680 --> 00:40:53,380
Why aren't you wearing one, though?

689
00:40:54,620 --> 00:40:55,460
Oh...

690
00:40:55,760 --> 00:40:58,470
Well, the time hasn't come yet,
and I'm in no rush.

691
00:41:27,820 --> 00:41:28,680
Let me see.

692
00:41:30,220 --> 00:41:33,560
So it's about ranks and all that.

693
00:41:53,540 --> 00:41:54,900
(May you always be lucky.
From Saming.)

694
00:42:34,680 --> 00:42:35,340
Hey.

695
00:42:35,830 --> 00:42:39,340
Belle is gonna stay at my place
during the long holiday.

696
00:42:39,490 --> 00:42:40,840
It'll be easier for me
to take care of her,

697
00:42:40,870 --> 00:42:42,660
and we'll get to see each other
more often.

698
00:42:44,110 --> 00:42:46,640
Who exactly is Belle?

699
00:42:47,710 --> 00:42:48,600
She's my ex-girlfriend.

700
00:42:49,160 --> 00:42:51,980
She's the one I loved most
and was closest to.

701
00:42:52,650 --> 00:42:55,210
We even almost got married,

702
00:42:55,520 --> 00:42:57,720
but she had plans to move overseas,

703
00:42:57,820 --> 00:42:58,910
so we had to call it quits.

704
00:43:00,610 --> 00:43:02,470
You never told me about any of that.

705
00:43:04,950 --> 00:43:07,530
It wasn't in the contract, was it?

706
00:43:13,020 --> 00:43:16,450
By the way,
she knows about our fake marriage.

707
00:43:17,440 --> 00:43:19,210
She just finds the whole thing funny.

708
00:43:23,180 --> 00:43:25,190
You seem to trust her a lot.

709
00:43:26,290 --> 00:43:27,550
I trust her
more than anyone in the world.

710
00:43:40,100 --> 00:43:41,230
Let me ask you something.

711
00:43:42,480 --> 00:43:44,390
When these six months are finally over,

712
00:43:44,760 --> 00:43:46,960
do you intend to keep living with me?

713
00:43:48,380 --> 00:43:50,530
Hey, I'm going to divorce you.

714
00:43:55,130 --> 00:43:56,530
Is it because of her?

715
00:43:57,440 --> 00:43:58,160
Well...

716
00:43:59,890 --> 00:44:01,100
That's part of it.

717
00:44:01,820 --> 00:44:04,030
You see, we made a promise

718
00:44:04,440 --> 00:44:06,750
that if neither of us
has found the right person yet,

719
00:44:07,030 --> 00:44:09,190
we would come back to each other.

720
00:44:16,160 --> 00:44:17,130
I see.

721
00:44:18,450 --> 00:44:19,410
So that means...

722
00:44:20,290 --> 00:44:22,540
you still haven't found
the right person, right?

723
00:44:24,360 --> 00:44:25,510
Not yet.

724
00:44:26,520 --> 00:44:28,670
I haven't found someone
who checks every single box.

725
00:44:29,230 --> 00:44:31,710
There are people
I'm comfortable being around,

726
00:44:32,870 --> 00:44:33,700
but I don't love them.

727
00:44:34,830 --> 00:44:36,070
But with Belle,

728
00:44:36,700 --> 00:44:38,080
she's everything.

729
00:44:42,510 --> 00:44:43,430
Okay.

730
00:44:46,690 --> 00:44:47,340
But...

731
00:44:48,030 --> 00:44:50,440
you should've figured that out sooner.

732
00:44:53,300 --> 00:44:54,270
I mean...

733
00:44:56,170 --> 00:44:57,830
You shouldn't have led me on.

734
00:44:59,350 --> 00:45:00,880
Look, I'm sorry. Okay?

735
00:45:01,430 --> 00:45:02,600
That's just the way I am.

736
00:45:02,720 --> 00:45:04,420
It's too late to change, you know.

737
00:45:07,110 --> 00:45:09,460
When I said I've been
having terrible luck lately...

738
00:45:11,440 --> 00:45:12,900
I don't think it's just bad luck.

739
00:45:14,820 --> 00:45:16,190
It's downright sh*tty luck.

740
00:45:20,170 --> 00:45:21,240
Look, come on.

741
00:45:21,940 --> 00:45:23,870
You'll be free in just a little while.

742
00:45:24,330 --> 00:45:27,450
If you want to keep staying at my place,
you're welcome to.

743
00:45:27,790 --> 00:45:29,990
It'll put my mom's mind at ease, too.

744
00:45:30,350 --> 00:45:31,410
I'd rather not.

745
00:45:32,100 --> 00:45:34,290
I don't want to be a third wheel to you.

746
00:45:36,610 --> 00:45:37,650
For now,

747
00:45:39,730 --> 00:45:42,100
I'll stay with Nadol.

748
00:45:49,170 --> 00:45:51,090
Next time, I hope
you realize your feelings sooner

749
00:45:52,980 --> 00:45:54,580
so that you won't waste anyone's time.

750
00:46:11,540 --> 00:46:13,050
It's better to laugh in a cramped space

751
00:46:13,820 --> 00:46:15,380
than to cry in a castle.

752
00:46:16,070 --> 00:46:17,610
I'll be troubling you
for a bit, Captain.

753
00:46:19,270 --> 00:46:21,100
I won't be here for too long.

754
00:46:22,320 --> 00:46:25,500
Tomorrow, I'll go file the paperwork
for my own room.

755
00:46:27,840 --> 00:46:28,890
So basically,

756
00:46:29,820 --> 00:46:31,170
from getting married for good luck

757
00:46:31,330 --> 00:46:33,070
to actually catching feelings, right?

758
00:46:45,950 --> 00:46:47,080
I hope you have a good night

759
00:46:48,350 --> 00:46:51,400
even if it might be hard to fall asleep.

760
00:46:55,410 --> 00:46:59,190
♪I know you're trying to ease the hurt,♪

761
00:47:02,990 --> 00:47:09,950
♪But all of this only makes it worse♪

762
00:47:10,250 --> 00:47:13,560
♪Let's stop wasting any more time,♪

763
00:47:13,950 --> 00:47:16,980
♪Avoiding it won't make things right♪

764
00:47:17,200 --> 00:47:19,090
♪Just end this, alright?♪

765
00:47:19,110 --> 00:47:22,090
♪Say I'm no longer the one in sight♪

766
00:47:22,110 --> 00:47:24,690
♪And that I've lost this fight♪

767
00:47:24,710 --> 00:47:28,310
♪I know what's going on, I fear♪

768
00:47:28,990 --> 00:47:31,830
♪Every move you've made makes it clear♪

769
00:47:32,100 --> 00:47:35,360
♪There's only one thing left
I need to hear,♪

770
00:47:35,540 --> 00:47:39,960
♪Just let your lips say it,
I'm all ears♪

771
00:47:40,140 --> 00:47:43,960
♪If you're leaving, just say it to me♪

772
00:47:43,990 --> 00:47:48,800
♪Don't make it harder than it has to be♪

773
00:47:48,830 --> 00:47:54,680
♪Just say you've already replaced me♪

774
00:47:55,160 --> 00:47:58,980
♪Just say it, what are you waiting for?♪

775
00:47:59,010 --> 00:48:03,170
♪Tell me it's over,
and I'll walk out the door♪

776
00:48:05,770 --> 00:48:10,330
♪Don't keep me guessing anymore♪

777
00:48:11,690 --> 00:48:13,450
- From this day forward,
- From this day forward...

778
00:48:13,770 --> 00:48:17,140
may there be
no more hardship or harm in our lives.

779
00:48:17,200 --> 00:48:21,640
And may we live happily
for many years to come.

780
00:48:25,160 --> 00:48:29,020
♪Just say it, what are you waiting for?♪

781
00:48:29,040 --> 00:48:33,220
♪Tell me it's over,
and I'll walk out the door♪

782
00:48:35,730 --> 00:48:40,170
♪Tell me all I need to know♪

783
00:48:41,770 --> 00:48:46,090
♪Don't keep me hanging anymore♪

784
00:48:49,280 --> 00:48:50,530
I think I'm in love
with Inspector Thear.

785
00:48:50,560 --> 00:48:51,730
It's time to call him yours

786
00:48:51,960 --> 00:48:53,350
and take him back.

787
00:48:54,180 --> 00:48:56,370
How's it going? Are they doing it?

788
00:48:57,890 --> 00:48:58,490
Where are you off to?

789
00:48:58,510 --> 00:49:00,120
We're going camping for a night.

790
00:49:02,840 --> 00:49:04,330
You're jealous of me and Belle,
aren't you?

791
00:49:04,590 --> 00:49:06,040
I'm sorry for upsetting you.

792
00:49:06,070 --> 00:49:07,370
Can you stay with me tonight?

793
00:49:12,850 --> 00:49:16,000
♪Let's stop wasting any more time,♪

794
00:49:16,610 --> 00:49:19,700
♪Avoiding it won't make things right♪

795
00:49:19,730 --> 00:49:21,690
♪Just end this, alright?♪

796
00:49:21,740 --> 00:49:24,770
♪Say I'm no longer the one in sight♪

797
00:49:24,810 --> 00:49:27,390
♪And that I've lost this fight♪

798
00:49:27,760 --> 00:49:31,580
♪Just say it, what are you waiting for?♪

799
00:49:31,610 --> 00:49:35,770
♪Tell me it's over,
and I'll walk out the door♪

800
00:49:38,360 --> 00:49:42,860
♪Don't keep me guessing anymore♪

801
00:49:42,880 --> 00:49:45,920
♪Say it and let me go♪

802
00:49:45,950 --> 00:49:49,800
♪Tell me all I need to know♪

803
00:49:51,940 --> 00:49:56,260
♪Don't keep me hanging anymore♪
